---
layout: layouts/product.njk
permalink: bikeright.html
app: bikeright
title: BikeRight – Safest Bike Route Navigation, Free on iOS
description: "Find the safest bike route using your city's real cycling infrastructure — every route safety-scored, with haptic turn-by-turn on Apple Watch. Free on iOS."
ogDescription: "Safer routes — every turn, and each segment's safety, called through your wrist. You don't read the safety score — you feel it."
lastmod: 2026-08-11
alternates:
  - { lang: en, href: "/bikeright.html" }
  - { lang: fr, href: "/fr/bikeright.html" }
  - { lang: de, href: "/de/bikeright.html" }
  - { lang: x-default, href: "/bikeright.html" }
---
{%- from "macros.njk" import appstoreBtn, screenshot -%}

    <!-- ── Hero ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="product-hero">
        <div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="container">
            <div class="product-hero-text">
                <h1>Get there on the streets that are actually built for bikes.</h1>
                <p class="product-hero-desc">Enter where you're going. BikeRight builds the route around protected lanes, quiet streets, and the cycling infrastructure your city actually has — then keeps your eyes on the road while you ride.</p>
                {{ appstoreBtn("https://apps.apple.com/app/bikeright-safer-bike-routes/id6759763484", "Download on the App Store", "bikeright") }}
            </div>
            <div class="product-hero-screenshot reveal">
                {{ screenshot("/screenshots/bikeright/02_route_selection", "BikeRight route selection with safety scores", 480, 1044, "(min-width: 1024px) 380px, 85vw", eager=true) }}
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Safety Score Visual ────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="safety-score-section reveal">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="safety-score-card">
                <p style="margin-bottom: 24px;">Every route comes with a safety score and a full breakdown — how much is protected bike lane, how much is shared road, and where the gaps are. Green is protected. Yellow is shared. You see it all before you ride — and feel it on your wrist once you're on the road.</p>
                <div class="safety-score-header">
                    <div class="safety-score-number">87</div>
                    <div style="flex: 1;">
                        <div class="safety-score-bar">
                            <div class="safety-bar-green" style="width: 62%;"></div>
                            <div class="safety-bar-yellow" style="width: 25%;"></div>
                            <div class="safety-bar-red" style="width: 13%;"></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="safety-score-legend">
                            <span class="safety-legend-item"><span class="safety-legend-dot safety-legend-dot--green"></span> Protected</span>
                            <span class="safety-legend-item"><span class="safety-legend-dot safety-legend-dot--yellow"></span> Shared</span>
                            <span class="safety-legend-item"><span class="safety-legend-dot safety-legend-dot--red"></span> Unprotected</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Why Not Google ────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="differentiator reveal">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="differentiator-inner">
                <blockquote>Google Maps finds the fastest route. BikeRight finds the one where you're not sharing a lane with delivery trucks.</blockquote>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── How It Works ──────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="how-it-works">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="how-section-header reveal">
                <span class="label">How it works</span>
                <h2>Plan the safest route. Ride it without looking.</h2>
            </div>

            <div class="steps-container">
                <div class="step reveal">
                    <div class="step-marker">
                        <span class="step-number">01</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="step-body">
                        <h3>Pick your destination</h3>
                        <p>Work, a friend's place, the other side of town — enter where you're headed and BikeRight does the rest.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="step reveal">
                    <div class="step-marker">
                        <span class="step-number">02</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="step-body">
                        <h3>See the safety breakdown</h3>
                        <p>Every route comes with a safety score: how much is protected bike lane, how much is shared road, and where the gaps are.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="step reveal">
                    <div class="step-marker">
                        <span class="step-number">03</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="step-body">
                        <h3>Ride without looking</h3>
                        <p>Every turn called through your wrist. Every segment's safety, too. Eyes on the road, hands on the bars.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Commuter Callout ──────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="feature-callout reveal">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="callout-box">
                <div>
                    <p><strong>Same commute, better streets.</strong> See the safety breakdown for your daily ride — or find a better one you didn't know existed.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Section Connector ─────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="section-route-connector" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 200 80" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <path class="route-line route-line--ride" d="M0,60 L30,60 L30,30 L70,30 L70,50 L110,50 L110,20 L150,20 L150,40 L200,40" stroke-width="2"/>
        </svg>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Screenshots ───────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="screenshots">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="screenshots-header reveal">
                <span class="label">See it in action</span>
                <h2>The whole ride, start to finish.</h2>
            </div>

            <div class="screenshots-grid">
                <div class="screenshot-card reveal">
                    {{ screenshot("/screenshots/bikeright/01_home", "BikeRight home screen", 480, 1044, "202px") }}
                    <div class="screenshot-caption">
                        <div class="screenshot-caption-title">Pick your destination</div>
                        <p class="screenshot-caption-desc">Enter where you're headed or set a distance for a loop.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="screenshot-card reveal">
                    {{ screenshot("/screenshots/bikeright/02_route_selection", "BikeRight route selection with safety scores", 480, 1044, "202px") }}
                    <div class="screenshot-caption">
                        <div class="screenshot-caption-title">See the safety breakdown</div>
                        <p class="screenshot-caption-desc">Each route scored and ranked. The safest option is always clear.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="screenshot-card reveal">
                    {{ screenshot("/screenshots/bikeright/03_live_map", "BikeRight live map with color-coded route safety", 480, 1044, "202px") }}
                    <div class="screenshot-caption">
                        <div class="screenshot-caption-title">Know before you ride</div>
                        <p class="screenshot-caption-desc">Green is protected. Yellow is shared. You see it all before you go.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="screenshot-card reveal">
                    {{ screenshot("/screenshots/bikeright/04_navigation", "BikeRight turn-by-turn navigation", 480, 1044, "202px") }}
                    <div class="screenshot-caption">
                        <div class="screenshot-caption-title">Turn-by-turn for cyclists</div>
                        <p class="screenshot-caption-desc">Speed, distance, time — all up front.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="screenshot-card reveal">
                    {{ screenshot("/screenshots/bikeright/05_ride_summary", "BikeRight ride summary screen", 480, 1044, "202px") }}
                    <div class="screenshot-caption">
                        <div class="screenshot-caption-title">Ride complete</div>
                        <p class="screenshot-caption-desc">Distance, time, average speed. Home safe.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Loop Feature ──────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="feature-callout reveal">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="feature-callout-inner">
                <p><strong>No destination?</strong> Set a distance and get a loop scored the same way — built around your city's best cycling infrastructure.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Ride Safe Intro ───────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="ride-safe-intro reveal">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="ride-safe-intro-inner">
                <span class="label">Ride Safe</span>
                <h2>The safest route is only as safe as how you follow it.</h2>
                <p>Pulling out a phone at every intersection means your eyes are on a screen instead of on traffic. BikeRight is built so you don't have to look down.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Feature Beat: Apple Watch ─────────────────── -->
    <section class="feature-beat reveal">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="feature-beat-inner">
                <div class="feature-beat-media">
                    <img src="/screenshots/bikeright/watch_haptic_nav-416.webp" alt="BikeRight Apple Watch app showing turn-by-turn navigation and upcoming-segment safety through haptic taps" width="416" height="496" loading="lazy">
                </div>
                <div class="feature-beat-text">
                    <span class="label">Apple Watch</span>
                    <h2>You don't read the safety score. You feel it.</h2>
                    <p>BikeRight on Apple Watch taps your wrist as each new segment begins — one tap for a protected lane, two for shared, three for unprotected, and a pair of four-taps when it's rough enough that you might want to look up anyway. The safety breakdown you saw on the map, delivered through your wrist while you ride.</p>
                    <p>The same wrist calls every turn. A tap pattern for left, another for right — you learn the rhythm in one ride and never forget it.</p>
                    <p><strong>No screen to check. No glance down.</strong> Eyes on the road. Hands on the bars.</p>
                    <p class="feature-beat-footnote">Standalone app. Works without your phone. Apple Watch Series 6 and later.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Feature Beat: Live Activity ───────────────── -->
    <section class="feature-beat feature-beat--reverse reveal">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="feature-beat-inner">
                <div class="feature-beat-media">
                    {{ screenshot("/screenshots/bikeright/live_activity", "BikeRight Live Activity on iPhone Lock Screen and Dynamic Island showing next turn while riding", 480, 1044, "(min-width: 1024px) 480px, 360px") }}
                </div>
                <div class="feature-beat-text">
                    <span class="label">Lock Screen &amp; Dynamic Island</span>
                    <h2>Phone in the mount? Don't touch it.</h2>
                    <p>Your next turn, distance to it, and the current segment's safety stay visible on the Lock Screen as a Live Activity. Dynamic Island keeps the turn in view even while you take a call or change music.</p>
                    <p><strong>One less reason to take a hand off the bars.</strong></p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Privacy ───────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="privacy-section">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="privacy-card reveal">
                <p>No account. No tracking. No ads.</p>
                <p>Your location never leaves your phone. Open the app and go.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Specs ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="specs-section">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="spec-grid reveal">
                <div>
                    <span class="spec-label">Platform</span>
                    <span class="spec-value">iOS 17.6+</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <span class="spec-label">Price</span>
                    <span class="spec-value">Free</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <span class="spec-label">Apple Watch</span>
                    <span class="spec-value">Standalone — haptic turns + segment safety</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <span class="spec-label">Live Activities</span>
                    <span class="spec-value">Lock Screen + Dynamic Island</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <span class="spec-label">Safety scoring</span>
                    <span class="spec-value">OpenStreetMap infrastructure data</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <span class="spec-label">Privacy</span>
                    <span class="spec-value">No account, no tracking</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
